Changelog: 01-11-2026 15:45:35

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 15:23:16

Fixed. The native core's GPU decoder test no longer takes an opened Direct3D device for decoding on the GPU: on
GitHub's runners the device opens but has no video decoder, and FFmpeg decodes in software, as it should (CI:
test_decoder_on_the_gpu_or_says_why failed). Each frame's picture now has to match where that frame was decoded.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 14:20:49

Added. The stream (owner, 01-11-2026: phase 2): A on a console of My consoles plays it, waking it when it rests,
full screen with the handheld's controls as the console's controller, until View, LB and RB are held for two seconds
(the suite's way out of a game, core's play mode) or the screen is touched and held. Console Link's native core
(native/, Rust) built for Windows with Rust's GNU toolchain and MSYS2's MINGW64 GCC, its FFmpeg decoding on the GPU
with Direct3D 11 (D3D11VA, else DXVA2) in place of VA-API (both of FFmpeg's D3D11VA hwaccels are needed: the decoders
offer the pixel format only with the older one); the controllers through SDL3 (SDL3.dll, pinned in binaries.toml);
the sound, the picture, the network test and the stream as Console Link has them. X opens a console's page: wake, test
session, test stream, the stream's settings stepped with A (resolution, frame rate, bitrate, picture, sound delay, low
latency), the login passcode, its Steam entry (Remote-Play.exe --stream <console>, the direct start, with artwork
drawn from the icon; Y takes it out), rest mode and remove on a second press. A History card lists the games played
and clears them. Each stream writes its statistics, with Windows' processor figures. Changes for Windows: the network
test times its pings with perf_counter (monotonic ticks every 15.6 ms on Windows, which measured a round trip as 0),
and so does the history's clock; the stream's files are in the app's %LOCALAPPDATA% folder.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 13:15:46

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 12:36:16

Added. Remote Play (apps/rplay, package remote_play, Gaming; owner, 01-11-2026): the BC250 Bazzite Suite's Console
Link made for the handheld, on the portable window, its steps before the stream. Four cards: Consoles (X searches the
network, Y one address typed on its row's page; A on a console chooses it for registering, or goes to it on My
consoles), Register (the console, the PSN account ID from the PlayStation sign-in in the browser, taken from the
clipboard as soon as the sign-in's last page's address is copied, or typed, and the console's PIN; X registers), My
consoles (A wakes, X tests a session, RB puts the console in rest mode and Y removes it, each of those two on a second
press, LB sets the login passcode) and Settings (the personal details shown or masked, and the log read in the app).
The protocol code is Console Link's, ported from chiaki-ng (AGPL-3.0), so the app is AGPL-3.0 too. One change for
Windows: a search at one address no longer ends at the "port unreachable" Windows hands to the next read
(WSAECONNRESET), and registration says nothing listens there as on Linux. The registered consoles and their keys are
in %LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\windows-portable-rplay\consoles.json, on this device only; uninstalling
keeps them, --purge removes them. The personal details are masked in the log, always.
